  "notes": "USAGE:\nAlmost always used with a negative nuance — warning someone not to believe something, or commenting that someone was naive to believe it. Common patterns include {真|ま}に{受|う}けないで (don't take it seriously) and {真|ま}に{受|う}けてはいけない (you mustn't take it at face value).\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {冗談|じょうだん}を{真|ま}に{受|う}ける: to take a joke seriously\n- {真|ま}に{受|う}けないで: don't take it seriously\n- そのまま{真|ま}に{受|う}ける: to take at face value as-is\n- {何|なん}でも{真|ま}に{受|う}ける: to believe everything",
